const guidebookHTML=`<section class="guide-entry"><h3>Getting started</h3><p>Choose a body area, read its comfort reminder, and begin with a short routine. A supported position matters more than completing every step.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Pressure guide</h3><p>Aim for light pressure that feels pleasant and easy to stop. Stronger is not automatically better. Never use pain as a measure of success.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Breathing guide</h3><p>Let breathing stay natural. You can breathe in gently and breathe out however feels comfortable. Do not hold your breath or force unusually deep breaths.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Creating a calming space</h3><p>Choose a stable seat or supported resting position. Reduce distractions if you want, keep water nearby, and make sure the room feels comfortable.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>When to stop</h3><p>Stop if a movement causes pain, numbness, tingling, dizziness, nausea, skin irritation, or any unfamiliar symptom. Do not continue over an injury, swelling, heat, bruising, or unexplained tenderness.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Building a habit</h3><p>A short routine is enough. Consider linking a brief pause to an existing moment, such as after school, after work, or before bed. Missing a day does not mean you failed.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Favorites</h3><p>Use the heart button to save routines you like. Favorites are stored locally in the current browser and are not attached to a cloud account.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Privacy basics</h3><p>This standalone app stores progress in this browser's local storage. Clearing browser data or using another browser may remove or hide the saved information.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Accessibility</h3><p>Use the keyboard to move between buttons and fields. Press Escape to close dialogs. Reduced-motion settings are respected where supported by the browser.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Routine customization</h3><p>If a step does not suit you, skip it. The timer is a suggestion and not a strict rule. You can end a session at any time.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Gentle self-talk</h3><p>Try replacing 'I have to relax' with 'I can take one comfortable breath.' Relaxation cannot be forced, and it is okay if your mind wanders.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Care around joints</h3><p>Avoid direct pressure on bony joints, the spine, the front or sides of the neck, and any area that is injured or painful. Use the area-specific safety note.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Skin comfort</h3><p>Use clean hands and avoid broken, irritated, infected, or inflamed skin. Stop if you notice redness or discomfort that does not quickly settle.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Health conditions</h3><p>If you have a health condition, recent surgery, reduced sensation, circulation concerns, are pregnant, or are uncertain about a technique, ask a qualified healthcare professional whether it is suitable.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section><section class="guide-entry"><h3>Progress without pressure</h3><p>The activity cards show a history of sessions completed in this browser. The numbers are not a score and do not say anything about your worth or health.</p><p>Remember: you are allowed to pause, change position, skip a movement, or stop. Your comfort is the most important part of this experience.</p></section>`;
const safetyText=`Sole Serenity offers general relaxation guidance only. It is not medical advice and is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent a condition. Use only comfortable, gentle touch. Stop immediately if you notice pain, numbness, tingling, dizziness, skin irritation, or any unusual symptom. Avoid massaging an area that is injured, swollen, hot, bruised, infected, or unexplainedly painful. Do not press on the front or sides of the neck, directly on the spine, or on bony joints. If you have a health condition, recent surgery, reduced sensation, circulation concerns, are pregnant, or are unsure whether massage is appropriate, ask a qualified healthcare professional first.`;
const aboutText=`Sole Serenity is a self-care companion built around gentle guided routines, timers, and personal progress. It does not replace professional care. Your favorites, settings, and session history are saved locally in this browser unless you clear browser storage. There is no sign-in, cloud sync, or online account in this standalone version.`;
