<!--
SOLE SERENITY EDITOR'S REFERENCE LIBRARY
This appendix documents the content structure for future edits. It is intentionally included in the single-file source so a beginner can inspect the area/routine organization without opening another file.

AREA: Arms & Hands
DESCRIPTION: Gentle care for hands, wrists, forearms, and upper arms.
SAFETY NOTE: Keep pressure light around the wrist and elbow; avoid pressing directly on joints.

ROUTINE: Soft Start: Arms & Hands
STYLE: A beginner-friendly sequence focused on comfort, gentle pacing, and noticing how you feel.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Settle your hand
GUIDANCE: Rest your arm on a pillow or table. Let your fingers loosen and take two easy breaths.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 2: Palm circles
GUIDANCE: Use the opposite thumb to make small, gentle circles in the center of your palm. Keep pressure pleasant.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 3: Finger glide
GUIDANCE: Lightly glide from the base of each finger toward its tip. Skip any sore finger.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 4: Forearm sweep
GUIDANCE: With an open palm, glide lightly along the forearm toward the elbow. Do not press on the wrist or elbow joint.
SUGGESTED TIME: 60 seconds
STEP 5: Wrist pause
GUIDANCE: Let the wrist rest in a neutral position. Make a tiny, comfortable circle only if it feels good.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 6: Finish softly
GUIDANCE: Rest both hands, release your shoulders, and notice whether your hand feels comfortable.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
REMINDER: Choose comfort over completion; skip any movement that does not feel right.

ROUTINE: Desk Break: Arms & Hands
STYLE: A short pause that can fit into a busy day without needing equipment.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Settle your hand
