AREA: Feet
DESCRIPTION: Slow, soothing routines for tired feet.
SAFETY NOTE: Avoid deep pressure if you have reduced foot sensation, an injury, or unexplained pain.

ROUTINE: Soft Start: Feet
STYLE: A beginner-friendly sequence focused on comfort, gentle pacing, and noticing how you feel.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Get comfortable
GUIDANCE: Sit down and support your foot. Make sure the position feels stable and relaxed.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 2: Sole glide
GUIDANCE: Use a light, comfortable glide along the sole. Avoid sharp pressure or painful spots.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 3: Arch circles
GUIDANCE: Make tiny circles around the arch with a thumb or knuckle only if it feels comfortable.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 4: Toe-by-toe
GUIDANCE: Gently hold each toe and make a small, easy movement. Never pull or force a toe.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 5: Top of foot
GUIDANCE: With light fingertips, glide across the top of the foot, avoiding strong pressure between bones.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 6: Rest and notice
GUIDANCE: Set the foot down and notice how it feels. Stop if numbness, pain, or tingling appears.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
REMINDER: Choose comfort over completion; skip any movement that does not feel right.

