AREA: Face
DESCRIPTION: Light, comfortable facial relaxation.
SAFETY NOTE: Use clean hands, feather-light pressure, and avoid the eyes or irritated skin.

ROUTINE: Soft Start: Face
STYLE: A beginner-friendly sequence focused on comfort, gentle pacing, and noticing how you feel.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Clean hands
GUIDANCE: Wash or sanitize your hands. Keep touch light and avoid irritated skin.
SUGGESTED TIME: 20 seconds
STEP 2: Forehead sweep
GUIDANCE: Use fingertips to glide gently from the center of the forehead outward, away from the eyes.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 3: Cheek circles
GUIDANCE: Make small, feather-light circles on the cheeks. Do not press on the eyeballs.
SUGGESTED TIME: 40 seconds
STEP 4: Brow release
GUIDANCE: Trace lightly above the eyebrows, staying away from the eyes and eyelids.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 5: Jawline glide
GUIDANCE: With a relaxed jaw, glide lightly along the jawline without digging into the tissue.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 6: Stillness
GUIDANCE: Rest your hands and allow the face to relax naturally.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
REMINDER: Choose comfort over completion; skip any movement that does not feel right.

