ROUTINE: Soft Start: Ankles
STYLE: A beginner-friendly sequence focused on comfort, gentle pacing, and noticing how you feel.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Support the foot
GUIDANCE: Sit with the foot supported and the ankle in a neutral, comfortable position.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 2: Light circles
GUIDANCE: Use fingertips to make tiny circles around—not directly on—a comfortable soft-tissue area.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 3: Above the ankle
GUIDANCE: Glide lightly along the lower leg, avoiding bruised, swollen, or painful spots.
SUGGESTED TIME: 45 seconds
STEP 4: Easy ankle movement
GUIDANCE: If comfortable, point and relax the foot gently without forcing the movement.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 5: Foot top glide
GUIDANCE: Use feather-light touch over the top of the foot, avoiding pressure between bones.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 6: Finish
GUIDANCE: Rest the foot. Do not continue if you notice pain, swelling, numbness, or tingling.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
REMINDER: Choose comfort over completion; skip any movement that does not feel right.

