AREA: Jaw Relaxation
DESCRIPTION: A mindful routine for unclenching and relaxing the jaw.
SAFETY NOTE: Do not force the mouth open. If jaw pain persists, ask a healthcare professional.

ROUTINE: Soft Start: Jaw Relaxation
STYLE: A beginner-friendly sequence focused on comfort, gentle pacing, and noticing how you feel.
LEVEL: Beginner
STEP 1: Let the teeth separate
GUIDANCE: Allow your lips to rest together while keeping the upper and lower teeth slightly apart.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 2: Temple circles
GUIDANCE: Use two fingertips to make small, very light circles at the temples.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 3: Cheek muscle
GUIDANCE: Rest fingertips on the cheek muscle in front of the ear and use gentle circles.
SUGGESTED TIME: 40 seconds
STEP 4: Slow breathing
GUIDANCE: Breathe normally and avoid clenching, stretching, or forcing your mouth open.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 5: Jaw awareness
GUIDANCE: Notice whether you are gripping your teeth. Let the jaw hang naturally without exaggerating.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
STEP 6: Finish softly
GUIDANCE: Release your hands. If jaw pain or locking persists, seek professional advice.
SUGGESTED TIME: 30 seconds
REMINDER: Choose comfort over completion; skip any movement that does not feel right.

